      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “novelty seeking” as a motivation to “look for new or different options.” It only refers to “novelty-seeking motivation” as a mediating factor between luck perception and variety-seeking, without stating the meaning of novelty seeking in those terms.",
        "The claim that novelty seeking “can increase preference for variety” is consistent with the packet (Experiment 2 and Experiment 1 link novelty-seeking motivation to variety-seeking), but because the core definition (“motivation to look for new or different options”) is not supported, the overall definition is not defensible."
